        "decision_frontier": "In the first goal-linked inquiry, discriminate reach/coverage limitation from stabilization limitation in the first learned policy. Evidence that separates them is a completed fixed-seed evaluation with per-episode target radius and angle, first in-tolerance step, maximum uninterrupted held steps, hold interruptions, and minimum/final distance, interpreted against the baseline training distribution and the official development distribution. Predominantly late first reach or geometry-correlated failures would support a coverage/trajectory direction; early reach followed by short holds and repeated interruptions would support a stabilization-aware learning direction. A mixed pattern would require identifying the dominant subgroup before intervention.",
